    section: "1", questionRef: "2024 HL Section 1 Q8",
    questionText: "Distinguish between two types of management control commonly used in a business.",
    tariffModel: {"kind":"bestNofParts","notation":"2@5m(3+2)","answer":2,"ofParts":4,"perPart":5}, totalMarks: 10,
    rows: [
    { id: "r-1", kind: "anyN", verbatim: "Quality Control / Credit control / Stock Control / Financial Control", marks: null, contextNote: "Two controls, 5m(3+2) each — the control named for 3 and distinguished for 2. \"quaintly\" in the stock control point is the scheme's own typo for quantity.", openList: true, group: {"claimMax":2,"perOption":5,"options":["Quality Control: Ensuring that the product and service standards expected by customers are properly met. Quality control involves regularly measuring the standards of the goods and services.","Credit control: Monitoring which customers are given credit, for how long and ensuring they pay it on time. Credit control involves checking the creditworthiness of debtors and putting in place measure to ensure prompt payments.","Stock Control: Ensures businesses have the right quaintly and type of goods in stock at the right time, without incurring stockholding costs. Stock control increases consumer satisfaction and reduces costs.","Financial Control: Financial control involves measuring the financial performance of the business against cashflow forecasts and budgets."]} },
    ],
