    id: "bus-2021-hl-s3-q1b", topicId: "business-0-13", conceptId: "ccpc-role",
    section: "3", questionRef: "2021 HL Section 3 Q1(B)",
    questionText: "Evaluate the role of the Competition and Consumer Protection Commission (CCPC).",
    tariffModel: {"kind":"fixed","notation":"3 x 6m (3+3) + Evaluation 2m","answer":null,"ofParts":null,"perPart":null}, totalMarks: 20,
    rows: [
    { id: "r-1", kind: "anyN", verbatim: "The three roles you wrote about: any three of the following", marks: null, contextNote: "The scheme prints 3 x 6m (3+3) beside this list: three roles, six for each, three for naming the role and three for the sentence developing it. A role named and left there stops at three, so tick an option only if you also wrote what it means.", openList: true, group: {"claimMax":3,"perOption":6,"options":["Informs the consumer: The CCPC provides consumers with information about their rights in relation to the purchase of goods and services, as well as financial services. They provide a website, a helpline, social media site and engage in radio and television advertising. They also produce a newsletter through a subscription service on their website.","Enforces consumer law: The CCPC is the statutory body responsible for enforcing all consumer laws. They issue compliance notices, on the spot fines, prohibition notices and produce a Consumer Protection List of all businesses who have breached consumer law.","Advise the Government: The CCPC advise the Government on consumer issues and recommend where consumers may need extra protection via legislation.","Conduct Research: The CCPC engages in research into consumer behaviour. They do this in order to advise consumers on how they can change habits and save money or receive better value for money, e.g. switching electricity supplier.","Educate consumers: The CCPC website has many tools for consumers to use to make more informed decisions. These include financial calculators, cost comparisons for various financial services, interactive quizzes etc.","Monitors Mergers & Acquisitions: To ensure fair competition in the market for consumers, the CCPC monitors all mergers and acquisition in Ireland. This is to ensure that there are no dominant businesses in particular markets."]} },
    { id: "r-2", kind: "criterion", verbatim: "Evaluation required.", marks: 2, contextNote: "The command word is Evaluate, and the scheme sets aside 2 of the 20 for the evaluation itself, printed in the Max Mark column as Evaluation 2m. It cannot print the wording because it depends on the judgement you reached, so claim these 2 only if your answer actually reaches a verdict on how well the CCPC does this work — an answer that only describes the six roles has not evaluated anything." },
    ],
