    stem: "People in Business. Read the information supplied and answer the questions which follow. Public service unions affiliated to the Irish Congress of Trade Unions overwhelmingly endorsed the new public service agreement. (Adapted from Independent.ie)",
    questionText: "Illustrate the impact of trade disputes on any three stakeholders.",
    tariffModel: {"kind":"bestNofParts","notation":"3 x 5m (2+3)","answer":3,"ofParts":6,"perPart":5}, totalMarks: 15,
    rows: [
    { id: "r-1", kind: "anyN", verbatim: "Any three stakeholders from the following", marks: null, openList: true, group: {"claimMax":3,"perOption":5,"options":["Suppliers: Suppliers can experience a decrease in sales and profitability as the business is closed for a period of time. i.e. the business will order less/no raw materials during a period of industrial action such as a strike.","Government: Decrease in tax revenue. The government will receive less tax revenue from PAYE and VAT when a business is on strike.","Consumers: Consumers might be unable to buy goods and services due to industrial action. This is an inconvenience due to the loss of a service/ being unable to access products. The consumer might decide to buy the product from a competitor.","Employees: During an industrial dispute the employees may suffer a loss of wages and the dispute can impact job security.","Investors: Dividends will potentially decrease for investors due to decreased profitability during industrial action.","Employer: Industrial action can damage the business’s reputation and lead to decreased sales and profitability."]} },
    ],
