          "alt": "Stimulus item beside Question 2 (Domestic Environment). The question-part marker \"(C)\" sits at the far left; centred at the top is the bold headline \"Hospitality, tourism and retail firms hold Dublin protest\". Below is a greyscale news photograph of a daytime street demonstration in Dublin: several dozen people in winter coats stand on a footpath between a red-brick Georgian terrace with sash windows and fanlight-arched doorways on the left, and a stone classical portico with fluted columns and a dark panelled door on the right; a television camera on a tripod with its operator is at the far left, and an ornate cast-iron lamp standard rises at the centre right. The demonstrators hold printed placards; the legible ones read \"Budget Ignored Small Business\", \"BUDGET 2025 FAILED TO DELIVER\" (several copies), \"NO VAT / NO VOTE!\", \"HOSPITALITY & TOURISM\" and \"DON'T LET THE HIGH STREET DIE!\", with further small placards beginning \"HOSPITALITY SMEs...\" too small to read in full. \"Adapted from rte.ie\" is printed at the bottom right. The photograph is whole and legible.",
