    paperFileid: "LC033ALP041EV",
    schemeCitation: "Marking points quoted from the SEC marking scheme, Business 2025 Higher Level — © State Examinations Commission.",
    id: "bus-2025-hl-s3-q7b", topicId: "business-4-14", conceptId: "new-product-development-stages",
    section: "3", questionRef: "2025 HL Section 3 Q7(B)",
    stem: "Glanbia acquired The Optimum Nutrition brand in 2008. This was part of a shift in focus towards consumer nutrition products.",
    questionText: "Illustrate four stages, apart from launch, that Glanbia may use for developing a new product.",
    tariffModel: {"kind":"bestNofParts","notation":"4 x 5m (2+2+1)","answer":4,"ofParts":6,"perPart":5}, totalMarks: 20,
    rows: [
    { id: "r-1", kind: "anyN", verbatim: "Stages, apart from launch, that Glanbia may use for developing a new product", marks: null, contextNote: "Every stage is 5 — 2 for naming it, 2 for explaining it, and 1 for a reference or example to Glanbia. The scheme prints “Reference/Example to Glanbia required.” under all six stages, Idea Generation included, so four stages named and explained with no Glanbia reference anywhere stops at 16 of the 20. Launch itself is ruled out by the question. The Idea Generation option reads short only because the rest of that stage could not be quoted with it: the scheme finishes it “It may come from internal or external sources. An idea may come from brain-storming.” Either of those is the explaining the second 2 pays for.", openList: true, group: {"claimMax":4,"perOption":5,"options":["Idea Generation: Initial ideas for the new product are created.","Product Screening: The ideas are vetted/sorted and the impractical and unworkable ideas are eliminated, leaving the most likely one for further examination and development. Reference/Example to Glanbia required.","Concept Development: This involves turning the idea into an actual product or service that will appeal to customers. This stage involves identifying features for the idea. A unique selling point (USP) is identified which will distinguish it from other products. Reference/Example to Glanbia required.","Feasibility Study: This is carried out to assess if a product is viable. It looks at whether it can be produced technically and will it be profitable. It answers question like: What demand is there? What will it cost etc? Reference/Example to Glanbia required.","Prototype Development: This is a sample or working model of a product. It is produced to see if a product can be made and what materials are required to make it. It can be used to test the product to see what improvements can be made. Reference/Example to Glanbia required Reference.","Test Marketing: The product is tested on a sample of consumers before going into full production. Reference/Example to Glanbia required Reference."]} },
    ],
