    rows: [
    { id: "r-1", kind: "anyN", verbatim: "Two methods of market segmentation, each named and explained", marks: null, contextNote: "Every method also needs your own example: the scheme prints 'Example Required.' under all four. The Demographic list in the scheme runs one item further than it does here, ending 'age, gender, family size, income, occupation.', and it carries a second point: 'For mass marketing demographic is one of the best ways as everyone has an age, gender and income.'", openList: true, group: {"claimMax":2,"perOption":7,"options":["Demographic segmentation: Analyses consumers according to age, gender, family size, income","Geographic segmentation: Analyses consumers according to location county/region/country etc. By using segments such as urban versus rural, north versus south, sea coasts versus interior, warm areas versus cold, the business can design a marketing strategy to satisfy the chosen target markets.","Psychological: Analyses consumers according to social status, lifestyle and personality type. Attitudes- concerns around production. Lifestyles – health conscious","Behavioural: Analyses consumer according to their knowledge of and attitude toward the use of the product, impulse buying/value for money (special prices), gift packs of him/her."]} },
    ],
